# Ignore local Claude Code state, but share the team's slash commands.
#
# Three lines are needed, in this order. `!/.claude/` first, because a developer's
# global gitignore may exclude `.claude` outright and git will not descend into an
# excluded directory — so no negation of a child can take effect until the
# directory itself is re-included. Then exclude the contents, then re-include just
# the commands. Keeps settings.local.json and worktrees/ local while sharing the
# commands, and does so without depending on anyone's global config.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/commands/
packages/mermaid/src/diagrams/CLAUDE.md
packages/parser/CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.mermaid.md
CLAUDE.mermaid.md
.envrc
AGENTS.alana.md
CLAUDE.alana.md
